    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228-a1">

                <pb facs="0415" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg355"/>

                <head>Mr. Hollister to Commodore Boggs.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation United States of
                                America,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port-au-Prince,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 18, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> From information which I have received
                    since I left your ship, I am compelled to enter my most earnest protest against
                    your leaving the American citizens in this city in this defenseless condition.
                    President Salnave threatens to burn the town, and I have good reasons to believe
                    that he intends to do it.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. H. HOLLISTER.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Commodore <hi rendition="#small-caps">Boggs,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United States Steamer Be Soto, Harbor of
                            Port-au-Prince.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
